(window.GROUP_QUIZZES=window.GROUP_QUIZZES||{})["intro-to-pa-profession-pa-intro-master-exam-form-a"]={"title":"Intro to PA Profession Comprehensive Master Exam — Form A","category":"Intro to PA","exam":"General","sem":"summer-1-2026","questions":[{"q":"Who is considered the 'father' of the PA profession and founded the first program at Duke in 1965?","choices":["Dr. Amos Johnson","Dr. Richard Smith","Dr. Charles Hudson","Dr. Eugene Stead"],"answer":3,"exp":"Dr. Eugene Stead, chair of medicine at Duke, is recognized as the \"father of the PA profession\" and founded the first PA program there in 1965. — Intro to PA Profession lecture — History of the PA Profession"},{"q":"The first PA class at Duke University consisted of four former members of which group?","choices":["Peace Corps volunteers","Navy corpsmen","Army medics","Air Force pararescue"],"answer":1,"exp":"The first PA class at Duke in 1965 consisted of four former Navy corpsmen, chosen for their military medical experience. — Intro to PA Profession lecture — History of the PA Profession"},{"q":"In what year did Dr. Charles Hudson first introduce the PA 'concept' in a speech to the AMA House of Delegates?","choices":["1965","1971","1955","1961"],"answer":3,"exp":"Dr. Charles Hudson, president of the NBME, first introduced the PA concept in a speech to the AMA House of Delegates in 1961, later published in JAMA. — Intro to PA Profession lecture — History of the PA Profession"},{"q":"Which historical non-physician provider originated in Russia and still exists today?","choices":["Village health worker","Officer de Santé","Feldsher","Nurse midwife"],"answer":2,"exp":"The feldsher is a non-physician provider that originated in Russia in the 1600s and still exists today. — Intro to PA Profession lecture — History of the PA Profession"},{"q":"Which rural North Carolina physician-and-assistant pair (Dr. Amos Johnson and Buddy Treadwell) served as a role model for the PA profession?","choices":["Two former U.S. Army medical corpsmen","A pharmacist and a technician","A public health nurse and a certified midwife","A physician and his doctor's assistant"],"answer":3,"exp":"Dr. Amos Johnson, a rural North Carolina physician, and his assistant Buddy Treadwell served as the physician-and-assistant role model that helped shape the profession's design. — Intro to PA Profession lecture — History of the PA Profession"},{"q":"The five stages of evolutionary development of the PA profession are Ideology, Implementation, Evaluation, Incorporation, and:","choices":["Maturation","Regulation","Certification","Consolidation"],"answer":0,"exp":"The five stages are Ideology, Implementation, Evaluation, Incorporation, and Maturation, using the memory hook \"I Implement Every Important Maturation.\" — Intro to PA Profession lecture — History of the PA Profession"},{"q":"During which stage did HMO research demonstrate a 76% 'substitutability factor' for PAs?","choices":["Maturation","Evaluation","Ideology","Implementation"],"answer":1,"exp":"The Evaluation stage is when HMO research examined cost-effectiveness and demonstrated a 76% \"substitutability factor\" for PAs. — Intro to PA Profession lecture — History of the PA Profession"},{"q":"The Medex model for PA education was developed by which physician?","choices":["Dr. Henry Silver","Dr. Hu Myers","Dr. Richard Smith","Dr. Eugene Stead"],"answer":2,"exp":"Dr. Richard Smith developed the Medex model for PA education at the University of Washington. — Intro to PA Profession lecture — History of the PA Profession"},{"q":"Colorado's Child Health Associate Program (1968) was developed by:","choices":["Dr. Amos Johnson","Dr. Charles Hudson","Dr. Henry Silver","Dr. Eugene Stead"],"answer":2,"exp":"Dr. Henry Silver developed Colorado's Child Health Associate Program in 1968. — Intro to PA Profession lecture — History of the PA Profession"},{"q":"The '4 pillars' of the PA profession include professional association, educational organization, national certification, and:","choices":["Malpractice coverage","Continuing education","State licensure","Program accreditation"],"answer":3,"exp":"The fourth pillar of the profession, alongside professional association, educational organization, and national certification, is program accreditation. — Intro to PA Profession lecture — History of the PA Profession"},{"q":"In 1997, the Balanced Budget Act allowed CMS reimbursement to PAs in all settings at what percentage of physician fees?","choices":["80%","100%","85%","75%"],"answer":2,"exp":"The 1997 Balanced Budget Act allowed CMS to reimburse PAs in all settings at 85% of the physician fee schedule. — Intro to PA Profession lecture — History of the PA Profession"},{"q":"In 2021, the AAPA House of Delegates officially changed the profession's title designation to:","choices":["Physician Associate","Associate Physician","Medical Practitioner","Physician Extender"],"answer":0,"exp":"In 2021 the AAPA House of Delegates voted to change the profession's title designation to Physician Associate. — Intro to PA Profession lecture — History of the PA Profession"},{"q":"By the end of 2025, approximately how many PAs were certified?","choices":["150,000","201,038","330,000","92,049"],"answer":1,"exp":"By the end of 2025, approximately 201,038 PAs were certified. — Intro to PA Profession lecture — History of the PA Profession"},{"q":"Optimal Team Practice (OTP) was passed by the AAPA House of Delegates in what year?","choices":["2021","2014","2010","2017"],"answer":3,"exp":"Optimal Team Practice (OTP) was passed by the AAPA House of Delegates in 2017. — Intro to PA Profession lecture — History of the PA Profession"},{"q":"The mission of the PA History Society (PAHx) is best described as:","choices":["Sharing the history of the PA profession","Nationally certifying individual PAs","Lobbying state and federal legislators","Formally accrediting PA education programs"],"answer":0,"exp":"The mission of the PA History Society (PAHx) is to share the history of the PA profession and show how PAs make a difference in society. — Intro to PA Profession lecture — History of the PA Profession"},{"q":"Which agency is the recognized accrediting body for PA educational programs?","choices":["ARC-PA","NCCPA","PAEA","AAPA"],"answer":0,"exp":"ARC-PA (the Accreditation Review Commission on Education for the PA) is the recognized accrediting body for PA educational programs. — Intro to PA Profession lecture — PA Organizations"},{"q":"ARC-PA was created in what year?","choices":["1994","1974","2001","2010"],"answer":2,"exp":"ARC-PA was created in 2001 as a free-standing accrediting agency. — Intro to PA Profession lecture — PA Organizations"},{"q":"Which organization administers the CASPA centralized application service?","choices":["PAEA","NCCPA","ARC-PA","AAPA"],"answer":0,"exp":"PAEA administers CASPA, the centralized application service for PA programs. — Intro to PA Profession lecture — PA Organizations"},{"q":"The PACKRAT and End-of-Rotation exams are assessment tools produced by:","choices":["ARC-PA","PAEA","FSMB","NCCPA"],"answer":1,"exp":"PAEA produces the PACKRAT and End-of-Rotation/End-of-Curriculum assessment exams used by PA programs. — Intro to PA Profession lecture — PA Organizations"},{"q":"Which organization is the ONLY nationally recognized certifying body for PAs?","choices":["AAPA","PAEA","ARC-PA","NCCPA"],"answer":3,"exp":"NCCPA is the only nationally recognized certifying body for PAs. — Intro to PA Profession lecture — PA Organizations"},{"q":"NCCPA was established in what year?","choices":["1972","1981","1965","1974"],"answer":3,"exp":"NCCPA was established in 1974. — Intro to PA Profession lecture — PA Organizations"},{"q":"The right to use the 'PA-C' designation is conferred by:","choices":["NCCPA","State medical boards","ARC-PA","AAPA"],"answer":0,"exp":"The right to use the \"PA-C\" designation is conferred by NCCPA upon successful certification. — Intro to PA Profession lecture — PA Organizations"},{"q":"Which of the following is a Certificate of Added Qualifications (CAQ) offered by NCCPA?","choices":["Surgical Pathology","Diagnostic Radiology","Emergency Medicine","Anesthesiology"],"answer":2,"exp":"Emergency Medicine is one of the Certificates of Added Qualifications (CAQs) NCCPA offers. — Intro to PA Profession lecture — PA Organizations"},{"q":"The policy-making body of the AAPA is the:","choices":["Judicial Affairs Commission","House of Delegates","Assembly of Representatives","Board of Directors"],"answer":1,"exp":"The House of Delegates (HOD) is the policy-making body of the AAPA. — Intro to PA Profession lecture — PA Organizations"},{"q":"The student delegation to the AAPA House of Delegates numbers how many delegates?","choices":["15","13","27","22"],"answer":3,"exp":"The student delegation to the AAPA House of Delegates numbers 22 delegates, the largest delegation in the HOD. — Intro to PA Profession lecture — PA Organizations"},{"q":"Which organization is the only one that represents PAs in the state of Florida?","choices":["SAAAPA","FSMB","FAPA","PAF"],"answer":2,"exp":"FAPA (Florida Academy of Physician Associates) is the only organization that represents PAs specifically in Florida. — Intro to PA Profession lecture — PA Organizations"},{"q":"AAPA student membership costs how much for the entire time enrolled in an accredited program?","choices":["$195","$75","$60","$100"],"answer":1,"exp":"AAPA student membership costs $75 for the entire time a student is enrolled in an accredited program. — Intro to PA Profession lecture — PA Organizations"},{"q":"The Physician Associate Foundation (PAF) primarily focuses on:","choices":["Program accreditation","Certification exams","Philanthropy and service","Legislative lobbying"],"answer":2,"exp":"The Physician Associate Foundation (PAF) primarily focuses on philanthropy and service, funding scholarships, grants, and outreach programs. — Intro to PA Profession lecture — PA Organizations"},{"q":"As of the lecture, ARC-PA publishes accreditation standards currently in which edition?","choices":["4th edition","5th edition","6th edition","7th edition"],"answer":2,"exp":"As of the lecture, ARC-PA's Accreditation Standards for PA Education were in their 6th edition, published September 2025. — Intro to PA Profession lecture — PA Organizations"},{"q":"The SAAAPA Student President holds what position within AAPA?","choices":["A seat on the AAPA Board of Directors","President of the PAEA Board","Chair of the AAPA House of Delegates","A voting member of the FSMB"],"answer":0,"exp":"The SAAAPA Student President holds a seat on the AAPA Board of Directors. — Intro to PA Profession lecture — PA Organizations"},{"q":"The PA professional competencies are organized into how many domains?","choices":["Four","Seven","Six","Five"],"answer":1,"exp":"The PA professional competencies are organized into seven domains. — Intro to PA Profession lecture — Professional Practice"},{"q":"The PA competencies were most recently revised in what year?","choices":["2017","2021","2014","2025"],"answer":1,"exp":"The PA competencies were most recently revised in 2021. — Intro to PA Profession lecture — Professional Practice"},{"q":"Which is one of the seven PA competency domains?","choices":["Financial management skills","Pharmacology mastery skills","Advanced surgical technique","Society and population health"],"answer":3,"exp":"Society and Population Health is one of the seven PA competency domains. — Intro to PA Profession lecture — Professional Practice"},{"q":"The PANCE consists of how many multiple-choice questions?","choices":["360","330","300","400"],"answer":0,"exp":"The PANCE consists of 360 multiple-choice questions. — Intro to PA Profession lecture — Professional Practice"},{"q":"What percentage of PANCE questions are surgical?","choices":["At least 20%","Exactly 50%","At least 10%","At least 30%"],"answer":0,"exp":"At least 20% of PANCE questions are surgical in content. — Intro to PA Profession lecture — Professional Practice"},{"q":"How many hours of CME must a certified PA earn every two years to maintain certification?","choices":["150 hours","75 hours","50 hours","100 hours"],"answer":3,"exp":"A certified PA must earn 100 hours of CME every two years to maintain certification. — Intro to PA Profession lecture — Professional Practice"},{"q":"Of the required CME hours, at least how many must be Category I?","choices":["50","75","25","100"],"answer":0,"exp":"At least 50 of the required 100 CME hours must be Category I. — Intro to PA Profession lecture — Professional Practice"},{"q":"A PA must recertify by examination every how many years?","choices":["It is not required","5 years","2 years","10 years"],"answer":3,"exp":"A PA must recertify by examination (PANRE or PANRE-LA) every 10 years. — Intro to PA Profession lecture — Professional Practice"},{"q":"Which recertification option involves 25 questions quarterly over 12 quarters, scored instantly?","choices":["PANRE-LA","The PANCE","The PANRE","PACKRAT"],"answer":0,"exp":"PANRE-LA involves 25 questions delivered quarterly over 12 quarters, with instant scoring. — Intro to PA Profession lecture — Professional Practice"},{"q":"Licensure is described as which method of professional regulation?","choices":["The least rigorous","A voluntary option","Equivalent to registration","The most rigorous"],"answer":3,"exp":"Licensure is described as the most rigorous method of professional regulation. — Intro to PA Profession lecture — Professional Practice"},{"q":"In Florida, PA licenses are valid for how long?","choices":["10 years","2 years","1 year","5 years"],"answer":1,"exp":"In Florida, PA licenses are valid for 2 years before renewal. — Intro to PA Profession lecture — Professional Practice"},{"q":"Which process verifies a provider's education and training via primary source?","choices":["Licensure","Privileging","Credentialing","Scope determination"],"answer":2,"exp":"Credentialing is the process that verifies a provider's education and training via primary source, mandated by bodies like the Joint Commission and NCQA. — Intro to PA Profession lecture — Professional Practice"},{"q":"Standard PA reimbursement under Medicare is generally what percentage of the physician fee?","choices":["50%","85%","13.6%","100%"],"answer":1,"exp":"Standard PA reimbursement under Medicare is generally 85% of the physician fee. — Intro to PA Profession lecture — Professional Practice"},{"q":"'Incident-to' billing reimburses at what rate?","choices":["13.6% of physician fee","100% of physician fee","85% of physician fee","50% of physician fee"],"answer":1,"exp":"\"Incident-to\" billing reimburses PA services at 100% of the physician fee, though it carries many restrictions and effectively hides the PA's role from the bill. — Intro to PA Profession lecture — Professional Practice"},{"q":"The Emergency Medical Treatment and Labor Act (EMTALA) was enacted in what year?","choices":["2010","1974","1997","1986"],"answer":3,"exp":"EMTALA (the Emergency Medical Treatment and Labor Act) was enacted in 1986. — Intro to PA Profession lecture — Professional Practice"},{"q":"Under EMTALA, a hospital must provide what to any individual requesting emergency care?","choices":["Completely free medical treatment","A medical screening exam","Immediate surgery","A specialist consult"],"answer":1,"exp":"Under EMTALA, a hospital must provide a medical screening exam (MSE) to any individual requesting emergency care. — Intro to PA Profession lecture — Professional Practice"},{"q":"Which type of malpractice policy requires 'tail coverage'?","choices":["Claims-made","Named-insured","Occurrence","Bundled"],"answer":0,"exp":"Claims-made malpractice policies require \"tail coverage\" because they only cover incidents while the policy is actively in force. — Intro to PA Profession lecture — Professional Practice"},{"q":"The primary goal of Optimal Team Practice is to:","choices":["Substantially raise average PA salary levels nationwide","Require physician co-signature on all notes","Remove burdensome administrative constraints on PA practice","Standardize PANCE examination content nationwide"],"answer":2,"exp":"The primary goal of Optimal Team Practice is to remove burdensome administrative constraints on PA practice. — Intro to PA Profession lecture — Professional Practice"},{"q":"An Accountable Care Organization (ACO) must have a minimum of how many patients to start?","choices":["5,000","10,000","1,000","2,500"],"answer":0,"exp":"An Accountable Care Organization (ACO) must have a minimum of 5,000 patients to start. — Intro to PA Profession lecture — Professional Practice"},{"q":"The World Health Organization defines interprofessional collaborative practice as multiple professionals working together with patients, families, caregivers, and:","choices":["Administrators","Insurers","Communities","Regulators"],"answer":2,"exp":"The WHO defines interprofessional collaborative practice as multiple health professionals working together with patients, families, caregivers, and communities to deliver the highest-quality care. — Intro to PA Profession lecture — Health Care is Teamwork"},{"q":"Which is a documented benefit of interprofessional collaboration?","choices":["Reduced patient compliance","Higher clinical error rates","Increased patient mortality","Decreased professional burnout"],"answer":3,"exp":"Decreased professional burnout is a documented benefit of interprofessional collaboration. — Intro to PA Profession lecture — Health Care is Teamwork"},{"q":"Which is listed as a challenge/barrier to effective interprofessional collaboration?","choices":["High overall staffing levels","Hierarchical power structures","Shared electronic records","Standardized rounding practices"],"answer":1,"exp":"Hierarchical power structures are listed as a challenge/barrier to effective interprofessional collaboration. — Intro to PA Profession lecture — Health Care is Teamwork"},{"q":"A CRNA is a nurse who has completed additional training to:","choices":["Interpret radiographs","Deliver babies","Perform surgery","Administer anesthesia"],"answer":3,"exp":"A CRNA is a nurse who has completed additional training to administer anesthesia. — Intro to PA Profession lecture — Health Care is Teamwork"},{"q":"A Licensed Practical Nurse (LPN) typically works under the supervision of a(n):","choices":["Physician","Physician Assistant","Registered Nurse","Pharmacist"],"answer":2,"exp":"A Licensed Practical Nurse (LPN) typically works under the supervision of a Registered Nurse (RN). — Intro to PA Profession lecture — Health Care is Teamwork"},{"q":"Which provider requires a PharmD degree and is licensed by a State Board of Pharmacy?","choices":["Pharmacy technician","Pharmacist","Medical assistant","Respiratory therapist"],"answer":1,"exp":"A pharmacist requires a PharmD degree and is licensed by a State Board of Pharmacy. — Intro to PA Profession lecture — Health Care is Teamwork"},{"q":"A Licensed Clinical Social Worker (LCSW) is specifically trained in:","choices":["Anesthesia","Psychotherapy","Physical rehabilitation","Radiologic imaging"],"answer":1,"exp":"A Licensed Clinical Social Worker (LCSW) is specifically trained in psychotherapy. — Intro to PA Profession lecture — Health Care is Teamwork"},{"q":"Which of the four tenets of patient-centered care emphasizes family beliefs and values?","choices":["Dignity and respect","Participation","Information sharing","Collaboration"],"answer":0,"exp":"Dignity and Respect is the tenet of patient-centered care that emphasizes honoring family beliefs and values. — Intro to PA Profession lecture — Health Care is Teamwork"},{"q":"PAs are said to practice 'anywhere there are':","choices":["Pharmacies","Hospitals","Physicians","Nurses"],"answer":2,"exp":"PAs are said to practice \"anywhere there are physicians,\" reflecting their broad presence across primary care, hospital, surgical, and specialty settings. — Intro to PA Profession lecture — PAs & Clinical Practice"},{"q":"Which is one of the '5 C's' describing primary care functions?","choices":["Coordinated","Curative","Corporate","Compulsory"],"answer":0,"exp":"Coordinated is one of the \"5 C's\" describing primary care functions, alongside Comprehensive, Continuous, Accessible, and Patient-centered. — Intro to PA Profession lecture — PAs & Clinical Practice"},{"q":"Per the lecture, the professionalism qualities described are also commonly called:","choices":["Technical skills","Hard skills","Soft skills","Clinical skills"],"answer":2,"exp":"The professionalism qualities described in the lecture are also commonly called \"soft skills.\" — Intro to PA Profession lecture — Professionalism"}]};
